+# Agent Note: profile fallback follows isolated package links
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-14-profile-fallback-follows-isolated-links.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+`healProfilesModuleFallback` promises a breadth-first walk over the installed CLI dependency graph so bare plugin names resolve from `$DSH_HOME/profiles/node_modules`. `packageDirFromAnchor` returned the visible top-level symlink for a package installed by pnpm's isolated linker. The next breadth-first step therefore computed Node search paths from the symlink location instead of the package's virtual-store location and could not see that package's own dependencies. A production-only CLI deployment linked direct CLI dependencies but omitted the transitive plugin roster owned by `dsh-base` and `dsh-web-app`, so Web profile startup reported many `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND` failures.
+
+## Decision
+
+`packageDirFromAnchor` resolves a candidate to its real directory when the candidate itself is a symbolic link. Direct package directories retain their existing path. Each subsequent breadth-first step therefore starts from the pnpm virtual-store package directory, where Node's parent walk reaches that package's isolated dependency links.
+
+The fallback continues to contain one flat link per discovered package and still uses first resolution wins. The change only repairs discovery of dependencies behind an installed package symlink.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Hoisting every production dependency.** This would make the current search accidentally succeed but would replace the documented isolated-linker support with a package-manager layout requirement.
+- **Adding every Web plugin to the CLI manifest.** This duplicates bundle dependency ownership, drifts whenever bundle composition changes, and does not repair other transitive dependency walks.
+- **Resolving every candidate unconditionally.** macOS temporary directories expose `/var` through `/private/var`; unconditional canonicalization would change returned paths for ordinary directories. Only symbolic package entries require canonicalization.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Production and source installations produce the same complete profile fallback despite different pnpm layouts. The resolver performs one `lstat` and, for symbolic package entries, one `realpath` per discovered dependency. User-managed profile dependencies and direct package directories keep their existing precedence and paths.
+
+## Testing
+
+`packages/boot/app-boot/tests/profile.spec.ts` stages an isolated virtual-store package with a top-level symlink and asserts that its transitive dependency appears in the fallback. Existing flat-layout, exports-map, replacement, and idempotence tests remain unchanged.
